# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers Static Assets. Parsed by the host and
# never served as a file itself.
#
# ⚠ Forcing HTTPS is NOT done here, and cannot be. Plain http:// answers 200
# instead of redirecting, which is what makes a browser say "Not secure" on a
# site that has had a valid certificate since the zone was created. A
# `_redirects` rule was tried and removed: Cloudflare's redirects file matches
# on path only, and lists domain-level redirects as explicitly unsupported. The
# fix is the zone-level toggle SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates -> Always Use HTTPS,
# which needs dashboard access the deploy token's zone:read does not grant. The
# HSTS header below only protects visitors who have already arrived over HTTPS
# once; it cannot help a first-time visitor who types the bare hostname.
#
# The policy is as tight as it is because the site earns it: no third-party
# script, style, font or beacon, no inline <script>, no inline event handler, no
# style="" attribute, and — via build.inlineStylesheets:'never' in
# astro.config.mjs — no inline <style> block either. So every source can be
# 'self' and nothing needs 'unsafe-inline'. Re-check this if that ever changes.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Content-hashed filenames, so the bytes behind a given URL never change.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
